  "basicsIntro": "Quick references for rhythm, meter, and notation.",
  "bpmBasicsTitle": "BPM",
  "bpmBasicsBody": "BPM means beats per minute. Use a slower BPM when learning a new pattern, then raise it gradually when your timing feels steady.",
  "timeSignatureBasicsTitle": "Time Signature",
  "timeSignatureBasicsBody": "The top number tells how many beats are in each bar. 4/4 is common for pop and practice exercises, while 3/4 often feels like a waltz.",
  "subdivisionBasicsTitle": "Subdivision",
  "subdivisionBasicsBody": "Subdivision controls how the beat is split. Quarter is simple and steady; eighth and sixteenth make the click feel more detailed.",
  "downbeatBasicsTitle": "Downbeat",
  "downbeatBasicsBody": "The downbeat is the first beat of a bar. A stronger first click helps you hear the shape of the measure instead of counting every beat equally.",
  "jianpuBasicsTitle": "Jianpu",
  "jianpuBasicsBody": "Jianpu uses numbers for scale degrees, such as 1 2 3 5 6. It is common in Chinese instrument learning and can be mapped to note names by choosing a key.",
  "westernNotationBasicsTitle": "Western Notes",
  "westernNotationBasicsBody": "Western note names use A-G. Sharps (#) raise a note by one semitone, and flats (b) lower a note by one semitone.",
  "easternNotationBasicsTitle": "Eastern Notes",
  "easternNotationBasicsBody": "Eastern notation uses Sa Re Ga Ma Pa Dha Ni, or S R G M P D N. In this app they map to C D E F G A B.",
  "octaveNotationBasicsTitle": "Octaves",
  "octaveNotationBasicsBody": "Use ' for a higher octave and comma for a lower octave. For example, C' is higher than C, and C, is lower than C.",
  "groupedNotesBasicsTitle": "Grouped Notes",
  "groupedNotesBasicsBody": "A space moves to the next beat. Notes without a space are played inside the same beat, so C D E FG puts F and G together on beat four.",
  "heldNotesBasicsTitle": "Held Notes",
  "heldNotesBasicsBody": "A dash (-) holds the previous note for another beat. For example, C - D E keeps C sounding through the second beat.",
  "scalePatternGenerator": "Scale Pattern Generator",
  "scalePatternDescription": "Create a clean scale pattern and send it to your note sequence.",
